<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31687" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ob-lĭnĭo</span></b> , ii, itum,
		4, v. a. (post-Aug. collat. form of oblino, q. v.),
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to bedaub,
				besmear</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">talearum capita misto fimo cum cinere oblinire,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					5, 9, 3</span></i>
			; so <i>fin.</i>; <i><span class="en">id. 12, 2,
				42</span></i>; <i><span class="en">12, 15,
			2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">12, 44,
			6</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si quis aliquem caeno, luto oblinierit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 47, 11, 1, § 1</span></i>
			: so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oblinierit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp. 230</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cinis oblinita,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 245</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to blot out</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">veritatem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. Spir. Sanct. 3, 10, 60</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
